{"id": "DezesK9zUot", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why do Hindus walk around a temple CLOCKWISE? 🛕 And why, in a Shiva temple, do you NEVER finish the circle? 🤯\n\n🔄 It’s called pradakshina. Dakshina means “right”: you walk with God on your right side, all the way round.\n☀️ East, then south, then west: the same path the sun takes across the sky every day.\n\nBut here’s the twist 👇\n💧 In a Shiva temple, the water poured on the Shiva linga (the abhishekam) flows out through a channel on the north side: the somasutra.\n🙏 That water is tirtha, holy. You never step over it. You walk round until you reach it, then turn back and go the other way.\n📜 The Shiva Rahasya says it plainly: “somasūtraṁ na laṅghayet”, do not cross the somasutra (Shiva Rahasya 7.26.80).\n\nNext temple visit, show your child 🙏\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods’ stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. 15K FAMILY DEAL: Books 1–3 for ₹350 (was ₹500), only till 25 Oct midnight. Comment FAMILY and we’ll DM you the deal, or tap the link in bio → rishikatha.com\n\n💬 Did YOU know this Shiva rule? Comment YES or NO!\n🔖 Save this for your next temple visit, and share it with someone who always walks the full circle.\n\n#pradakshina #parikrama #shivatemple #shivling #mahadev harharmahadev hindutemple templerules sanatandharma hinduism hindutraditions kidsbooks rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792688808, "like_count": 39538, "comment_count": 201, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1630013391952534a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 53.298, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQN5bhWSrzyqwcu0xSKkxtN9OYVUDtiIRYudVtNAeS2-NcoXKMmwyRWVhxij9N3_4FReyEzJ0RobttlI6rjk0kkM8Yj_TjQyJ-7w0wk.mp4?_nc_cat=100&_nc_oc=AdqFJUI